Package: voxtype
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, curl
Recommends: wtype, wl-clipboard, voxtype-osd-gtk4 (= ${binary:Version})
Suggests: ydotool, libnotify-bin, pipewire
Description: Push-to-talk voice-to-text for Linux
 Voxtype is a push-to-talk voice-to-text daemon for Linux.
 Optimized for Wayland, works on X11 too.
 Hold a hotkey while speaking, release to transcribe and output text at
 your cursor position.
 .
 Features:
  - Works on any Linux desktop using kernel-level input (evdev)
  - Fully offline transcription using whisper.cpp, plus Parakeet and
    Cohere GGUF models through transcribe.cpp
  - On-screen waveform while recording (voxtype-osd)
  - Fallback chain: wtype (Wayland, CJK support), ydotool (X11), clipboard
  - Configurable hotkeys, models, and output modes
 .
 Note: User must be in the 'input' group for hotkey detection.
 .
 This package includes the AVX2 and Vulkan builds, the GGUF
 workers, the OSD launcher, the Quickshell OSD frontend and its audio
 bridge, OSD styles and the Omarchy Settings plugin. The GTK4 OSD frontend
 is in voxtype-osd-gtk4.

Package: voxtype-osd-gtk4
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, voxtype (= ${binary:Version})
Description: GTK4 waveform OSD for Voxtype
 The GTK4 frontend for voxtype-osd: a layer-shell overlay that shows the
 recording waveform. voxtype-osd uses it automatically when it is
 installed and falls back to the other frontends when it is not.
